FONT LICENSES
=============

This file records the license of every font artifact in this repository. There
are two kinds, both from the same upstream and both under the SIL Open Font
License, Version 1.1, whose full text follows this header.

The first kind is the three unmodified upstream TTF files committed under
tools/fonts/upstream/. They are IBM Plex release files shipped verbatim -
byte-identical to the GitHub release assets identified below - and therefore
keep their original IBM Plex names. Nothing in the firmware embeds them; they
are committed so the second kind can be regenerated reproducibly.

The second kind is the generated glyph atlases, crates/notyas-fonts/src/gen/
(one Rust source file per font and pixel size). Each atlas is produced from
one committed TTF by tools/fonts/atlasgen (run via tools/fonts/regen.ps1),
which subsets to the characters this device renders (U+0020-U+007E, U+2022,
U+2026) and rasterizes each glyph at a fixed pixel size into an 8-bit alpha
coverage bitmap plus an integer metrics table. These atlases are what the
firmware embeds and redistributes.

The atlases are Modified Versions, as OFL 1.1 defines that term: subsetting,
rasterization to bitmaps, and porting to a new format all qualify. Because
"Plex" is a Reserved Font Name declared in the upstream copyright line, OFL
clause 3 forbids a Modified Version from carrying that name, so the derived
families are renamed:

    IBM Plex Sans (Regular, SemiBold)  ->  notyas Sans (Regular, SemiBold)
    IBM Plex Mono (Regular)            ->  notyas Mono (Regular)

Every generated atlas file carries a header naming its upstream file, release,
and font version, this renaming, and a pointer to this file; the upstream
copyright notice below and this license accompany the atlases wherever they
are distributed, as OFL clause 2 requires.


